+# Assumptions Registry
+
+*Durable assumptions schedule per enacted law (Act 16 §2). Each entry records
+load-bearing claims, the observable evidence that would falsify each, and a
+review date. This is the standing input to the Judiciary's review and to
+Act 10/13 sunset logic.*
+
+## Index
+
+| Bill ID | Law | Assumptions File | Review Date | Status |
+|---------|-----|------------------|-------------|--------|
+| epistemic-adversarialism-act | Act 16 | [epistemic-adversarialism-act.md](epistemic-adversarialism-act.md) | 2026-10-24 | ACTIVE |
+
+## Plan for Remaining Enacted Laws
+
+The following enacted laws still require assumptions schedules. They will be
+added in priority order (by enactment date, oldest first):
+
+1. Act 1 (Parliament) — foundational; assumptions about quorum and voting
+2. Act 2 (Executive) — foundational; assumptions about clerk/executive roles
+3. Act 3 (Town Hall) — assumptions about Founder communication trust model
+4. Act 4 (Research and audit) — assumptions about audit independence
+5. Act 5 (Durability and restart) — assumptions about 24h restart cycle
+6. Act 6 (Legislation and publication) — assumptions about enactment process
+7. Act 7 (First agenda) — assumptions about inaugural parliament tasks
+8. Act 8 (Founding Service Priorities) — assumptions about Founder priorities
+9. Act 9 (Productive scope by assignment) — assumptions about assignment mechanism
+10. Act 9.7 (Territorial administration) — assumptions about box jurisdiction
+11. Act 11 (Model Compliance Audit) — assumptions about model verification
+12. Act 12 (Janitor Office) — assumptions about resource safety
+13. Act 13 (Resource Safety) — assumptions about memory headroom
+14. Act 14 (Legislative Innovation Centre) — assumptions about Centre autonomy
+15. Act 15 (Judiciary Independence) — assumptions about non-voting judiciary
+
+**Target completion:** 2026-10-24 (before Act 16 review date)
+
+## Maintenance
+
+- New enacted laws MUST have an assumptions schedule before or at enactment.
+- The Judiciary reviews this registry during each audit cycle.
+- Assumptions that are falsified MUST be recorded with evidence and the law
+  reconsidered at the next sitting.
